WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.132
Keep retriever inputs narrow and typed.

00:00:03.132 --> 00:00:12.987
A search tool might need only three values: the query, a small top K value, and perhaps an approved department filter.

00:00:12.987 --> 00:00:17.777
Avoid passing one giant arbitrary dictionary of arguments.

00:00:17.777 --> 00:00:23.534
That makes validation harder and gives the model too many ways to produce malformed input.

00:00:24.097 --> 00:00:31.648
For example, you might define query as a non-empty string, top K as an integer between one and ten,

00:00:31.648 --> 00:00:35.468
and department as an optional approved category.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:41.228
Typed schemas improve reliability because the model knows what fields exist,

00:00:41.228 --> 00:00:45.971
and the application can reject invalid values before touching the database.

00:00:46.639 --> 00:00:52.583
A small input schema is easier to generate, easier to test, and safer to execute.
